-- Record of a forward change already applied to production (KickON) on 2026-11-22 around 12:15 KST
-- through the SQL Editor. This file is a record, not an approval to run it (see README.md).
--
-- Why: after the override correction (20261122130000), 12 players still showed as
-- PLAYER_STATS_PROJECTION_MISMATCH. For all 12, both app tables equal the K League official record
-- (kleague.com, read 2026-11-22) and Sportmonks differs. Gangwon Kim Dae-won, for example, has 34
-- appearances and 10 goals officially, while Sportmonks reports 34 and 11.
-- Change: add 12 verified_official rows. Each is tied to that player's current Sportmonks snapshot
-- hash and date of birth, with verified_at 2026-11-22T02:45:00Z. A new snapshot or a later lineup
-- appearance expires the row as before. No other part of the function changes.
--
-- Verification on production: a pg_temp copy was compared with the deployed function. All output
-- except the projection check was identical. Projection errors went from kleague 2 / kleague2 10 to
-- none, and provider disagreements from 11 / 44 to 13 / 54. The first comparison used a future
-- verified_at (03:30Z, before the DB clock reached it) and matched nothing; it was corrected to 02:45Z.
-- The admin sync screen now shows the team season stats job as a provider disagreement, not an error.
--
-- Definition before: md5 8ddae6802cfd410a2b585d93ea6cadc9.
-- Definition after: md5 977d9be9ed067c03f1bd9d1de776a820,
-- sha256 7d33ecbcc04c7b8f9f01ff0ba2e00ebe0d63be341e09ec33bf6aea0c09fc9017.

